# Files NOT copied into the Docker build context.
#
# Reduces build-context upload size and prevents host-only paths (`.venv/`,
# `__pycache__/`) from leaking into the image. The runtime images are
# copy-explicit (`COPY dashboard ./dashboard` not `COPY . .`), so this list
# is mostly defense-in-depth — anything not COPY'd is already excluded —
# but the bytes still get sent to the daemon during `docker build`, so
# trimming them speeds up rebuilds noticeably on a populated `data/` tree.

# Generated / runtime artifacts
data/
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.cmem-archive/

# Dev tooling state
.git/
.github/
.claude/
.vscode/
.idea/

# Test scaffolding (the runtime image doesn't run tests)
tests/

# Node-side artifacts that aren't part of the dashboard image
ai_analyzer/node_modules/

# Editor / OS noise
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Docs that don't belong in the image
README.md
REFACTOR_AND_DASHBOARD_PLAN.md
CLAUDE.md
docs/
